# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor
.DS_Store

# Tool caches
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
# XLA kernels the suite compiled last run; see `tests/conftest.COMPILATION_CACHE`
.jax_cache/

# packaging build artifacts
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/

/graphify-out/

# driver outputs and their inputs. Every driver defaults under results/, and
# rank_targets --fetch writes depositions to data/; both are rebuildable from
# the recorded arguments, which is the point of writing those down.
#
# results/ IS the paper's evidence and is tracked, so a number in the manuscript resolves to a file
# anyone can open. Tracked by EXTENSION at any depth, not by listing directories: the rule was
# `results/*` plus `!results/*.json`, which re-included the top level only. Git does not descend into
# an excluded directory, so seven subdirectories -- every cryoSPARC chain record, and the 66-row
# rigour batch -- were ignored rather than untracked, which means `git status` never mentioned them.
# `_hb_prep_compare.sh` globs `results/cs_hb_rt/*.json`, a directory that had never been committed.
#
# The .npy log-ratio arrays are tracked too, 13.2 MB across 269 files. They are the REPLAY substrate:
# the whole-repo audit re-derived every recorded result from stored arrays instead of booking cluster
# time, and `memorization_law.py` takes its standard error from the array rather than the summary.
# The cost is binary churn whenever a run is repeated, which is the price of a replayable record.
#
# Everything else under results/ stays out, which is the 27 MB reference volume in cs_e9_spcas9.
results/**
!results/**/
!results/**/*.json
!results/**/*.npy
!results/**/*.md
# data/ is bulk deposited structures (gitignored); a few small ones are tracked as test fixtures.
/data/*
!/data/pdb/
/data/pdb/*
!/data/pdb/2OO8.pdb
!/data/pdb/6Z4Q.cif
!/data/pdb/8S4D.cif
!/data/pdb/8WJ1.pdb
!/data/pdb/8WJ2.pdb
!/data/pdb/9BA0.cif
/banks/
/logs/

# built artifacts, regenerated by docs/manuscript/build.py. The figures go with the docx for the same
# reason the result JSONs do NOT: a .json is a measurement nothing can recompute without the cluster,
# where a panel is a pure function of tracked results and a tracked script, and rebuilds in seconds.
# Tracking them would also churn a binary on every build.
docs/manuscript/manuscript.docx
# the citeproc rendered-bibliography preview (build.py --citeproc); regenerable, same as manuscript.docx
docs/manuscript/manuscript-citeproc.docx
docs/manuscript/figures/
# main.md with its <!-- figure-legends --> marker replaced from captions.md. Tracking it would put
# every caption in the repository twice, which is the drift the splice exists to prevent.
docs/manuscript/main.rendered.md
docs/manuscript/appendix.rendered.md
# Word's lock file, present whenever the docx is open; it is not ours and must not be tracked
docs/manuscript/~$*
.coverage

# transient worker locks from the convergent survey
results/kc_survey/*.lock
docs/manuscript/figures/values/

# superseded surveys, EMPIAR fetch receipts and old Slurm logs, kept on disk but untracked; outside
# results/ so tests/test_results_tracked.py still sees anything new that results/ silently ignores
/archive/

# exploratory Fig 5 planning plots (not manuscript figures)
docs/planning/figure5_*.png

# local pre-rescore safety copies of the half-map pools, kept on disk but not tracked
results/cas9_halfmap_backup/
results/ribo_pools_halfmap_backup/
